@startuml

title 12.3. Workflow status drift and history completion

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

class StatusTransitionService <<service>>
class BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer <<service>>
class InventoryPostingService <<service>>
class OrderHistoryRecorder <<history>>
class GenericStatusHistoryRecorder <<history>>
class InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition <<definition>>
class WorkflowDriftTestSuite <<tests>>

entity Order
entity Purchase
entity InventoryDocument
entity ProductionOrder
entity OrderHistory
entity StatusHistory

StatusTransitionService --> OrderHistoryRecorder : order transitions
StatusTransitionService --> GenericStatusHistoryRecorder : generic transitions
BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer --> Order : derived status
BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer --> Purchase : derived status
InventoryPostingService --> InventoryDocument : post/cancel status
InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition --> GenericStatusHistoryRecorder : future direct workflow
WorkflowDriftTestSuite --> StatusTransitionService
WorkflowDriftTestSuite --> BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer
WorkflowDriftTestSuite --> InventoryPostingService

note right of StatusTransitionService
  Current status:
  - Universal workflow core exists.
  - Order, Purchase and ProductionOrder definitions exist.
  - InventoryDocument implements WorkflowSubjectInterface.
  - InventoryDocument post/cancel history is recorded directly
    in InventoryPostingService, not via an InventoryDocument definition.

  Required cleanup:
  - Either add InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition or document that posting
    is a specialized workflow owned by InventoryPostingService.
  - Keep history recording exactly once for every post/cancel/reversal.
end note

note right of BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer
  Current status:
  - Purchase derived statuses now write StatusHistory when context exists.
  - Order derived statuses still use Order.setStatus directly and should
    write OrderHistory when they change.

  Required cleanup:
  - Add OrderHistory recording for derived order status changes:
    awaiting_stock, ready_to_ship, partially_shipped, shipped,
    partially_returned, returned.
  - Keep delivered/completed as explicit business actions, not inferred.
  - Add tests that direct status drift is visible in history.
end note

note right of InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition
  Optional implementation:
  - post: draft -> posted
  - cancel_draft: draft -> canceled
  - cancel_posted: posted -> canceled with reversal side effect

  Caveat:
  Stock posting contains heavy domain logic and transaction boundaries.
  If added, the workflow definition should delegate to actions/services,
  not move posting math into the generic transition service.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation order:

  1. Add OrderHistory recording inside BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer
     for derived Order status changes.
  2. Add tests for status history/order history on every automatic status
     change caused by inventory posting and reversal.
  3. Decide whether InventoryDocument gets a formal workflow definition.
  4. Add a static/targeted test that flags direct setStatus calls outside
     approved construction, synchronizer, posting and workflow actions.
end note

@enduml
